 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? That' usually the chain rubbing on the sprockets. Does it happen right after you stop pedalling, like when stop at red? Hang the bike upside down, loop a wire through the link, and push it through the big ring. Then hook it on a hook or a seatpost. Cleaning it with a brush and some dirt off wash is fine. Don't wash it with water, it can swell the oil.",
